 "title": "The “Unknome",
 "hook": "The human genome has been sequenced, but what do all those genes do? João J. Rocha et al.’s Unknome database assigns a “knownness” score to “all protein clusters that contain at least 1 protein from humans or any of 11 model organisms.” The score is based on the density of annotations in the Gene Ontology…",
